course: dictionary
lesson: 16047
title: Viewers and viewing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A viewer is a person who watches something. Most often it means someone watching television, a video or a show. «Millions of viewers watched the final match on Sunday night.» Here the viewers are the people watching the match on their screens.
explain: The word can also mean someone who looks at a painting or a view. «The viewers stood in a quiet line to see the painting.» The words around it are the clues: stood in a line and see the painting tell you the people are looking at art, not a screen.
explain: Look at the ending. Viewers ends in -s, so it means more than one person. Ask yourself: is the sentence about one viewer or a group? If it says «the viewers» or «young viewers», it means a group.
fact: A viewer is a person who watches something, such as a TV programme or a video.
fact: «Viewers» is the plural of «viewer», so it means more than one person.
fact: «TV viewers» means people who watch television.
fact: A viewer can also be a device or program for looking at pictures or files, such as a photo viewer on a computer.
fact: Numbers of viewers show how popular a show is.
exercise: «Millions of viewers watched the final on Sunday night.» Who are the viewers in this sentence? | People who play in the match | *People who watch the show | People who sell tickets | People who cook food
exercise: «The viewers stood in front of the painting.» What were the viewers doing? | Selling the painting | Cleaning the gallery floor | *Looking at the painting | Painting a picture
exercise: Which word is the plural of viewer? | *viewers | viewing | viewed | viewable
test: Adverts try to persuade young viewers to buy the new toy. What are young viewers? | Children who make adverts | *Children who are watching a show or advert | Children who sell toys | Children who are asleep
test: «The photo viewer on the computer opened my pictures.» What is a photo viewer? | A printer for paper pictures | A bag for carrying photos | *A program for looking at pictures | A camera for taking photos
exam: Which phrase means people who watch a show on television? | *TV viewers | Gardeners | Shop assistants | Bus drivers
